# KS-1015 delegation-get - GET /api/delegations/{id} publishes the success/data envelope its handler returns

File: `Blockchain/Dev/services/transfer/src/transfer.openapi.ts`  (product, modified in place: ONE one-line replacement at `:1196`, the line becomes 23 lines)
Test file: `Blockchain/Dev/services/transfer/src/__tests__/ks1015-delegation-get-spec-declares-envelope.test.ts`  (NEW, 79 lines)
Tip: `88e8877a2a0d6a626b9c2a7c4b71d3a909e6f94e` (origin develop, GitHub REST `GET /branches/develop` 2026-10-02 06:0x AEST; #1369). `transfer.openapi.ts` there is 1333 lines.
Runner: `vitest` (transfer service, `vitest run`, `vitest.config.ts` with `globals: true`, environment `node`, include `src/**/__tests__/**/*.test.ts`)

Written 2026-10-02 06:14 AEST by a Spark brief-writer sub-agent for Wednesday (session 73252fd5), from `88e8877a`, `transfer.openapi.ts` read at every line named here and the handler read. Source: KS-1015 (In Progress, assigned to Kamil; created by Peter 2026-09-08), its comment of 2026-09-29 12:49Z ("Sweep 2026-09-29: two more untriaged pairs"), which names `response_schema_conformance::GET /api/delegations/{id}` with "the handler returns the standard `{ success, data: {...} }` envelope, while the spec declares a flat object that requires `id`". The other pair of that comment, `GET /api/referrals/{code}`, landed as #1367 (`ed268a995`); this brief is its sibling, same shape.

## The mode - read this twice

CODE+TEST. Your diff touches EXACTLY 2 files, in this order:
1. `Blockchain/Dev/services/transfer/src/transfer.openapi.ts` - modified in place, `--- a/Blockchain/Dev/services/transfer/src/transfer.openapi.ts` / `+++ b/Blockchain/Dev/services/transfer/src/transfer.openapi.ts`, EXACTLY the 1 hunk given below, byte for byte.
2. `Blockchain/Dev/services/transfer/src/__tests__/ks1015-delegation-get-spec-declares-envelope.test.ts` - a NEW file: `--- /dev/null` then `+++ b/Blockchain/Dev/services/transfer/src/__tests__/ks1015-delegation-get-spec-declares-envelope.test.ts`, ONE hunk `@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@`, every line `+`.

You never touch any other file. The `reference_test_file` in your input (the referral service's KS-1015 spec test, landed in #1367) is shape reference only - do NOT touch it.

## What is wrong (one paragraph)

The registration for `GET /api/delegations/{id}` (`transfer.openapi.ts:1185`-`:1206`) declares its 200 body as the bare `DelegationSchema` component (`:1196`: `content: { 'application/json': { schema: DelegationSchema } },`), so the published spec says the 200 body is a flat Delegation record that requires `id`, `delegatorId`, `delegateId` and the rest at the top level. The handler says otherwise: `routes/delegations.ts:138` (`router.get('/:id', ...)`) answers `res.json({ success: true, data: { delegation, chain } })` (`:148`-`:154`), where `chain` is what `delegationService.buildDelegationChain()` returns (`services/delegationService.ts:430`-`:476`: `{ rootDelegatorId, chain, totalDepth, isValid, invalidReason }`; type `DelegationChain` at `types/delegation.types.ts:77`-`:83`, `invalidReason?` optional). The router is mounted at `index.ts:441` behind `jwtAuthenticate()` (`:438`). KS-1015's 2026-09-29 sweep recorded the pair as `response_schema_conformance`. The direction for this class (KS-1015 fix direction 3, the KS-591 direction, and the #1367 precedent in the same sweep comment) is that the spec follows the runtime. The file already wraps every other delegation 200 in `successEnvelope(...)` (`DelegationListResponseSchema` `:620`-`:624`, `DelegationDocumentListResponseSchema` `:694`-`:701`, `DelegationCreateResponseSchema` `:768`-`:775`), and `successEnvelope` is already imported (`:45`).

## Where

- `:1196` - the GET /api/delegations/{id} 200 `content:` line; it is REPLACED by the 23 lines below (replacement site)

